# The three loops over the index space compute from the index (and an
# offset) alone, so their bodies only compute; after idr-vectorize they
# run on the target's lanes, and after idr-narrow-lanes each loop that
# computes 64-bit lanes is the 64-bit version beside one computing them in
# 32 bits, under a bound on n and the offset that this fixture's input is
# below (linarray-lanes-narrow) or above (linarray-lanes-wide), a negative
# offset above it either way: both versions must give Chez's numbers.
idr-rc: pure-array-loops
idr-vectorize: vectorized
idr-narrow-lanes: narrowed-lanes
